Article 5 (Duties of Security Management Personnel)
(1) Security management personnel shall comply with statutes and regulations and faithfully perform their duties in accordance with instructions from the overall officer in charge and on-site managers.
(2) Security management personnel shall not engage in any of the following acts:
1. Conduct undermining the dignity of security management personnel, including violence, insulting language or conduct, or sexually discriminatory or harassing language or conduct;
2. Leaving the workplace without permission from the overall officer in charge or an on-site manager;
3. Smoking, idle conversation, drinking alcohol, sleeping or other conduct that interferes with faithful performance of duties while on duty;
4. Wearing attire that violates the applicable regulations;
5. Other conduct that violates statutes or regulations or matters prescribed by the head of the establishing agency.
(3) The head of an establishing agency shall have the overall officer in charge and on-site managers supervise the performance of duties and service of security management personnel and shall ensure that appropriate measures can be taken where they violate their duties.
